Q: How to click on the Hcaptcha using puppeteer-extra A: <p>Your selector is fine. The issue is the hcaptcha is inside an iframe. <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/59433663/6243352">Expand the iframe</a> before clicking:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const puppeteer = require(&quot;puppeteer&quot;); // ^24.36.1
const {setTimeout} = require(&quot;node:timers/promises&quot;);

let browser;
(async () =&gt; {
  browser = await puppeteer.launch({headless: false});
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  await page.goto(&quot;https://accounts.hcaptcha.com/demo&quot;, {
    waitUntil: &quot;networkidle0&quot;,
  });
  const checkboxFrame = page.frames().find(f =&gt;
    f.url().includes(&quot;frame=checkbox&quot;)
  );
  await checkboxFrame.click(&quot;#checkbox&quot;);
  const challengeFrame = page.frames().find(f =&gt;
    f.url().includes(&quot;frame=challenge&quot;)
  );
  await challengeFrame.waitForSelector(&quot;.refresh&quot;);
  await setTimeout(2_000); // TODO use a tighter predicate
  await page.screenshot({path: &quot;challenge.png&quot;});
})()
  .catch(err =&gt; console.error(err))
  .finally(() =&gt; browser?.close());
</code></pre>
<p>The separate challenge frame contains the challenge itself.</p>
<p>Note that while selectors <em>could</em> be different on prod captchas, the CSS selectors or even the click itself isn't really the protection. It's the captcha problem itself.</p>
